    {
      "id": "node-1782589526659-0.42569515607556374",
      "type": "canvas_note",
      "position": {
        "x": 2080,
        "y": -140
      },
      "style": {
        "width": 1180,
        "height": 175
      },
      "width": 1180,
      "height": 175,
      "data": {
        "label": "Note",
        "params": {
          "color_index": 5,
          "text": "**MC Water Mask — Threshold-Free Extraction by Topological Persistence**\n\nThe whole challenge of this study is to *avoid arbitrary thresholds*. A binary cut at P≥0.5 is a guess. Here we replace it with **0-D persistent homology** of the probability map.\n\n1. `geo_persistence` sweeps the super-level sets of P. Each candidate water body is born at its peak P and dies when it merges into a more persistent neighbour at a saddle. Its **persistence** (peak − saddle) measures how robustly it survives across *all* thresholds.\n2. The significance cut is **auto-detected** from the largest gap in the persistence spectrum — no value chosen by hand. Real lakes (high persistence) separate cleanly from speckle (low persistence, near the diagram diagonal).\n3. **Bottom branch** contrasts the topological mask with a naive fixed P≥0.5 cut, so you can see what the threshold choice costs.\n\nOutputs: persistence saliency map (colormap in the node body), persistence diagram (scatter), threshold-free water mask, and stats."
        }
      },
      "selected": false,
      "positionAbsolute": {
        "x": 2080,
        "y": -140
      },
      "dragging": false
    },
